{
  "abstract": "The inclusive cross sections, measured up to large values of effective mass (\u2261q22\u03bd), are well fitted by d\u03c3d3p=Bxexp(\u2212\u03b1xp22mx). Values of Bx and \u03b1x are given for Be, C, Cu, and Ta at the incident proton energy of 600 MeV and for Ag, Ta, and Pt at 800 MeV. Extremely large dp and tp ratios and large A and q2 dependences of the relative cross sections are observed.",
